<section aria-labelledby="m-what">
  <h2 id="m-what">What the milestone calculator shows</h2>
  <p>Milestone birthdays are the ages people plan around — 18 and 21, the decade birthdays, 65 and 100. For each one, the calculator gives the date, the weekday and how many days it is from the selected date, marking it as reached, today or upcoming. It also shows day-count milestones — 1,000, 5,000, 10,000 days old and so on — which rarely coincide with a birthday.</p>
  <p>The timeline places every age milestone and the 10,000-day mark around the selected date, so you can see at a glance what has passed and what comes next. Enter a custom age (1–150) to add any other milestone.</p>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="m-ex">
  <h2 id="m-ex">Example</h2>
  <p>For someone born on 15 January 1990, viewed on 26 September 2026: they turned 30 on 15 January 2020 and passed 10,000 days old on 2 June 2017. Their next milestone is age 40 on 15 January 2030, 1,207 days away; 20,000 days old falls on 18 October 2044, and age 65 on 15 January 2055.</p>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="m-rule">
  <h2 id="m-rule">How milestone dates are calculated</h2>
  <p>An age milestone is the birthday in the year the person reaches that age: the birth date plus that many calendar years. A day-count milestone is the birth date plus that many days, which is why 10,000 days lands at roughly 27 years and 4 months rather than on a birthday. For a birth date of 29 February, an age milestone in a common year is placed on 28 February by default or 1 March if you choose that rule.</p>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="m-elig">
  <h2 id="m-elig">Milestones are dates, not eligibility decisions</h2>
  <p>Many rules are tied to an age — voting, driving, retirement benefits, school entry — but each authority defines its own cut-off, and some use a date other than the birthday. The calculator tells you when you reach an age; it does not decide whether you qualify for anything. Check the official source for the rule that applies to you.</p>
  <p>To see your exact age today, use the <a href="/date-of-birth-calculator/">Date of Birth Calculator</a>. For a simple countdown to your next birthday, try the <a href="/birthday-countdown-calculator/">Birthday Countdown Calculator</a>.</p>
</section>
